# Protected trunk workflow

## Status

Accepted — {{DATE}}

## Context

{{PROJECT_NAME}} needs a reviewable mainline workflow that keeps `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` releasable,
works with {{MAINTAINER_COUNT}} active maintainer(s), and does not spend the full quality matrix on
documentation-only changes.

## Decision

- Use `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` as the only long-lived integration branch.
- Require Pull Requests, a unique `required` status context, resolved conversations, linear
  history, and a current branch tip.
- Include administrators and prohibit force pushes and deletion.
- Allow only squash merge and delete merged head branches.
- Run an always-emitted lightweight gate; conditionally skip language-specific jobs for
  documentation-only paths.
- Use {{REQUIRED_APPROVALS}} required approval(s).
- Treat tags and Releases as explicit delivery events rather than side effects of every merge.

## Alternatives considered

### Long-lived develop branch

Rejected unless the project later has a release-train requirement that cannot be handled with
short-lived topic and release branches.

### Skip the complete workflow for documentation

Rejected because a path-skipped workflow may never report a required status context.

### Multiple merge methods

Rejected because one reviewed PR should map predictably to one mainline commit.

## Consequences

- Every mainline change has a PR audit trail.
- Code PRs may rerun after `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` advances.
- Documentation PRs still run lightweight jobs but skip the expensive quality matrix.
- Changes to the `required` job name must be coordinated with repository protection settings.
